## Diagram Generation Instructions

Based on the code analysis above, create a comprehensive {{diagramType}} diagram:

{{#if (eq diagramType "uml")}}
### UML Class Diagram:
- Show classes with attributes, methods, parameters, and return types
- Display relationships: inheritance, composition, association, aggregation, dependency
- Include multiplicities (1, *, 0..1, 1..*, etc.) and visibility modifiers (+, -, #)
- Use standard UML notation: group related classes, position base classes above derived
- Show interfaces, abstract classes, and stereotypes with proper notation
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq diagramType "flowchart")}}
### Flowchart Diagram:
- Show execution flow from start to end with all major processes
- Display decision points (diamonds), loops, and conditional branches
- Include error handling paths, data I/O, and user interaction points
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq diagramType "sequence")}}
### Sequence Diagram:
- Show participants/actors with lifelines, displaying user interactions and system responses
- Display method calls and messages chronologically with return messages
- Include activation boxes, synchronous/asynchronous calls, and conditional fragments (alt, opt, loop)
- Show object creation/destruction where applicable
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq diagramType "erd")}}
### Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD):
- Show entities with attributes, data types, primary keys (PK), and foreign keys (FK)
- Display relationships with cardinality (one-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-many)
- Include participation constraints, unique constraints, indexes, and weak entities
{{/if}}

